@* =============================================================================
   SECTION 22: SHARED LAYOUT — NAVIGATION TAG HELPERS
   =============================================================================
   FILE ROLE: Application-wide layout shell that wraps every view rendered by
              this project.  Demonstrates anchor tag helpers (asp-action,
              asp-controller, asp-route-*, asp-route, asp-area) for generating
              navigation URLs through the routing engine rather than hard-coding hrefs.
   =============================================================================

   ANCHOR TAG HELPER (AnchorTagHelper):
     Transforms <a> elements by replacing the href attribute with a URL generated
     by IUrlHelper — the same engine used by Url.Action inside controllers.
     The tag helper activates ONLY when asp-action or asp-route is present.

     Attributes:
       asp-action       — target action method name
       asp-controller   — target controller name (without "Controller" suffix)
       asp-area         — target area name; use "" to explicitly leave an area
       asp-route-{name} — any additional route value; e.g. asp-route-id="5"
       asp-route        — generate URL using a NAMED ROUTE directly
       asp-fragment     — URL fragment appended after #
       asp-protocol     — protocol override (http / https) for absolute URLs
       asp-host         — hostname for absolute URLs

   GENERATED HTML EXAMPLES:
     <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Home</a>
     → <a href="/">Home</a>

     <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Details" asp-route-id="5">Product</a>
     → <a href="/products/5">Product</a>   (attribute route: [controller]/{id:int})

     <a asp-route="product-detail" asp-route-id="7">Named</a>
     → <a href="/products/7">Named</a>     (bypasses controller/action lookup)

   AMBIENT ROUTE VALUE WARNING:
     When the current request is inside an area, the area name is "ambient".
     An <a> without asp-area="" INHERITS the ambient area value and may produce
     links pointing INTO the current area instead of to the root app.
     Always write asp-area="" explicitly when linking out of an area.

   TAG HELPER vs HTML HELPER EQUIVALENTS:
     Tag helper:  <a asp-action="About" asp-controller="Home">About</a>
     Html helper: @Html.ActionLink("About", "About", "Home")
     Tag helper syntax is preferred: reads like HTML, integrates with editor tooling.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>@ViewData["Title"] — Routing Demo</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 0; color: #222; }
        nav { background: #1a1a2e; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
        nav a { color: #e0e0e0; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.88rem; }
        nav a:hover { color: #fff; text-decoration: underline; }
        main { max-width: 960px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
        h1 { color: #1a1a2e; border-bottom: 2px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
        h2 { color: #333; margin-top: 2rem; }
        h3 { color: #555; }
        table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
        th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; text-align: left; }
        th { background: #f0f0f0; font-weight: 600; }
        tr:nth-child(even) { background: #fafafa; }
        code { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.85em; font-family: monospace; }
        .url-demo { background: #f8f8f8; border-left: 3px solid #1a1a2e; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; margin: 0.4rem 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
        .url-demo a { color: #0066cc; }
        em { color: #666; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<nav>
    @* asp-controller + asp-action — the most common tag helper combination for navigation *@
    <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Home</a>                @* → /  (conventional default route) *@

    @* ProductsController is attribute-routed; tag helper still generates the correct URL *@
    <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Index">Products</a>        @* → /products  (attribute route) *@

    @* Blog is conventionally routed (no class-level [Route] on BlogController) *@
    <a asp-controller="Blog" asp-action="Index">Blog</a>                @* → /blog  (conventional default route) *@

    @* asp-route-id — passes the "id" route value; the tag helper appends it to the template *@
    <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Details" asp-route-id="1">Product #1</a>      @* → /products/1 *@

    @* asp-route — uses the named route "product-detail" directly (bypasses controller/action lookup) *@
    <a asp-route="product-detail" asp-route-id="2">Product #2 (named)</a>                  @* → /products/2 *@

    @* URL Demo action on HomeController — conventional route *@
    <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="UrlDemo">URL Demo</a>          @* → /home/urldemo *@
</nav>
<main>
    @RenderBody()
</main>
</body>
</html>
